WEBVTT

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:06.020
It's time for B Block in 
the WRGP final tournament!

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.860
The final tournament is between the eight 
teams that passed the preliminaries.

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:18.390
In A Block, Team New World showed their 
overwhelming power to advance to the A Block finals!

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.990
It's time.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:35.810
Team 5D's, you must win 
and stop Iliaster's plans!

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.010
What?

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.340
They don't have a single rare card?

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:40.210
Yeah.

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:44.030
All the cards in their deck are Normal Cards.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:48.170
Can I have your autograph?

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.640
I'm surprised they made it through 
the preliminaries with that deck.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:57.550
They may be trying to trick us.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:59.900
They showed Yusei a weak deck on purpose.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:00.890
That's not true!

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.730
Taro wouldn't do that!

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.210
I know that more than anyone!

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:13.500
Anyway, Team Taiyo isn't 
worthy of being our opponent.

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:17.910
We'll face our real opponent in 
the second round!  Team Ragnarok!

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.660
Just wait, Team Ragnarok!

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:31.840
Let me introduce the two teams 
in B Block's first match!

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.570
First, the powerful team that passed the

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:37.540
preliminaries by defeating Team 
Unicorn and Team Catastrophe!

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:39.440
Team 5D's!

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.450
Jack!

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:47.920
Master Atlas!

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:54.870
They're facing an unknown team that 
advanced to the final tournament.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:57.650
Team Taiyo!

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.900
We have to face each other eventually.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.600
It just happens to be the first match.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.510
So let's duel our best so that 
we have no regrets later.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:15.570
Yeah!

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.950
Do your best, Team Taiyo!

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.300
Do your best!  Hang in there!

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.570
Thank you!

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:28.390
We really made it.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.490
Yeah.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.930
WRGP?

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:41.240
Yeah!

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:45.910
The World Riding Duel Grand Prix decides 
who's the world's best riding duelist!

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.250
Riding Duels.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:53.350
These duels evolved in the world of speed.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:03:00.260
The people with the legendary marks who 
risked their lives were known as 5D's.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:21.480
Reach out your hand and 
grab a bright tomorrow

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:31.590
Soar in the infinite skies  BELIEVE IN NEXUS

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:37.830
No one can stop my wild impulses

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:43.800
My hand sweats as the battle 
intensifies  This Heart Beat

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:49.570
I can't avoid this fearsome battle

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:55.180
I don't want it to end here  Go For It!!

00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:01.550
Stand up  Don't tremble in fear alone

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:07.360
Remember that you have 
friends waiting for you

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:13.670
I'm not scared and I'll never give 
up, no matter how powerful the enemy

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:19.970
With real courage, I'll never lose

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:50.570
Steel Wall Scrum!
Destroy the Impenetrable Defense!

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.880
World Riding Duel Grand Prix?

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:02.250
Taro, is something wrong with you?

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:06.150
A Riding Duel requires cards and a D-Wheel.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:09.980
We don't have cards nor a 
D-Wheel, so how can we enter?

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:12.320
You don't have to worry about that.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:15.450
I found someone who will sell us a D-Wheel.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.820
And we can work together to collect cards.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:20.090
Let's enter, Jin.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.130
Forget about it.

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:27.340
Even if we enter, there's no way we 
can win against the world's best.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.250
That might be true, but...

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:33.060
I really want to enter.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:36.720
I don't care if we lose in our 
first match.  I still want to try.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.970
It's not that I hate working at home.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:45.880
Every morning, I milk the cows.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.610
I'm fine with that.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:51.230
But I always feel depressed.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:55.910
I feel like I'm forgetting to do 
something before it's all over.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:01.290
When I saw this ad, something hit me!

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:04.580
That this is what I want to do!

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.340
So won't you enter with me?

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:14.320
You said that it's no fun living in the 
outskirts if you don't have dreams.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:17.020
You want to go to the city 
and do incredible things!

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:20.240
I'll enter.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:24.920
If I enter that GP thing, 
I can go to the city.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:27.270
There are a lot of beautiful women there.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:28.300
You idiot!

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.260
Ouch!

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.040
Please, Jin!

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:35.200
Just once, I want to do 
something with all my heart!

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:37.290
Jin!

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.180
I'll think about it.

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:43.390
Thank you, Jin!

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:47.190
Let's go pick up that D-Wheel!

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:50.330
This is the D-Wheel?

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:00.990
Good luck.

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:04.700
I think he tricked us.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:07.450
We'll have to fix it.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.330
There are a lot of things to fix.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.770
Hey!

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:18.080
I picked these up.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.160
Thank you!

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:25.470
It's still no good.

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:49.550
Dad.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:52.010
Can you fix it?

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:56.230
Well, all the parts are rusted.

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:57.940
Come with me.

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:10.700
A D-Wheel!

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:13.500
This is in better shape than yours.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:16.320
If you can fix it, it should run.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:17.860
Dad…

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:20.820
I'm sorry that I never told you.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:25.180
I felt that if I showed you, you would leave.

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:27.220
But if that's what you 
want to do, that's fine.

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:29.110
Dad.

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:32.790
Don't worry.

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:35.820
I'm not going anywhere.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:39.560
I'm entering the WRGP 
so that I can stay here.

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:41.100
Stay here?

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:46.270
That's why I want to know how far I can go.

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:47.720
Taro...

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:54.900
All right, it's done!

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.320
Let's test it!

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:57.450
Yeah!

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:04.820
It started!  Hooray!

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:08.280
Our D-Wheel is finally complete!

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:13.440
That's still not enough.

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:15.910
Here.

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:22.310
The cards I collected 
today were also garbage.

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:25.160
We can't win with these cards.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:30.720
That's not true.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:33.050
Every card is useful in a duel.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.240
Haven't you had enough?

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:46.700
This card is also Level 1.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:49.930
Give up!

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:53.970
We're not good enough for the WRGP anyway!

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:55.410
Hey, Jin!

00:09:58.100 --> 00:09:59.980
Is it really impossible?

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:06.950
That's it!

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:12.010
There's a dueling style that only we can do!

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:19.180
It's true that we only have Normal 
Cards that aren't special.

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:22.330
But since we have a certain 
card, we can fight.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.890
A single card of hope.

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:29.060
The first D-Wheelers Jack and 
Yoshizo are at the starting line.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:30.910
The match is about to begin!

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:34.610
Hey, can that D-Wheel really run?

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:37.550
I think this battle will be over in a snap.

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:41.180
Don't hold back!  Beat them quickly!

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:45.230
Leave it to me!  I'll end this duel quickly!

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:48.560
It doesn't matter how they duel.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:51.260
We just have to execute our own duel.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:55.010
Duel Mode on.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:58.330
The match is about to begin!

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:04.340
Go, go, let's go, fight!

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.310
Riding Duel!

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:11.130
Acceleration!

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:13.550
What?

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:16.200
Team Taiyo erupts from the starting line!

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:17.980
All right, Yoshi!

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:20.970
That D-Wheel is better than I thought.

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:25.980
What did Bruno and Yusei 
do to that piece of junk?

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:29.600
Still, it's no match for Wheel of Fortune!

00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:33.510
Wheel of Fortune accelerates!

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:38.560
All right, Jack!  Pass him!

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:45.710
Both teams simultaneously 
enter the first corner!

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.040
I won't lose!

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:51.930
Team Taiyo lost his balance!

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:58.500
But he keeps going!  Team 
Taiyo takes the first corner!

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:03.610
All right, we go first!

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.560
You amateur!

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:09.720
Duel!

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:16.460
My turn!

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:19.970
I summon Key Mace from my 
hand in defense position!

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:24.950
Key Mace?

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:30.190
Whoa!  Team Taiyo summons a Level 1 
Normal Monster in defense position!

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:32.670
They're going to fight with that card?

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:36.270
The deck Yusei saw was real.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:40.230
That means they won the preliminaries 
using only Normal Cards.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:43.370
I'm excited to see how they duel.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:04.850
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:09.310
That weak monster can't stop my attack!

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:11.070
My turn!

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:14.600
I summon Twin-Sword Marauder!

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:22.350
When this card attacks a 
monster in defense position...

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:26.750
...it deals piercing damage if it has more 
attack points than your monster's defense points!

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:29.130
Key Mace has 300 defense points.

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:31.460
He'll take 1300 points of damage!

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:33.420
I activate the trap Hidden Soldiers!

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:36.760
When you summon a monster, 
I can Special Summon a

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:40.160
Level 4-or-below Dark Attribute 
monster from my hand!

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:43.150
I Special Summon Hand-Holding 
Genie in defense position!

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:54.640
This card gains defense points equal to the total 
defense points of my monsters in defense position!

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:56.780
All right!

00:13:56.970 --> 00:14:01.420
Hand-Holding Genie's defense points are 
greater than Twin-Sword Marauder's attack points!

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:09.130
And when Hand-Holding Genie is faceup on the 
field, you can't attack any other monster!

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:12.090
This prevents Twin-Sword 
Marauder from attacking.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:18.640
Twin-Sword Marauder attacks 
Hand-Holding Genie.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:32.140
Jack Atlas knew that he would take 
damage, but he still attacked!

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.620
What's going on?

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:37.380
When my Warrior-Type monster 
fails to destroy your

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:42.300
monster in battle, I can Special 
Summon this card from my hand!

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:45.070
I Special Summon Sword Master!

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:53.000
I set one card and end my turn.

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:58.740
He's planning to defeat him quickly.

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:02.180
Yeah.  Red Dragon Archfiend 
will appear on the next turn.

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:03.920
It's a Synchro Summon.

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.650
Synchro Summon?

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:10.420
That's why Jack attacked a monster 
with higher defense points.

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:13.660
He did that so he could Special Summon 
the Tuner Monster Sword Master.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:15.220
I see!

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:18.180
Bring it on!  My turn!

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:22.080
I summon Genin in defense position!

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:27.520
Another monster in defense position?

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:34.300
Due to Hand-Holding Genie's effect, it gains 
defense points equal to Genin's defense points!

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:37.240
I set one card and end my turn!

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:41.230
Hand-Holding Genie's defense 
points increase to 2800.

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:44.060
He's tightening his defense.

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:47.590
It's not a bad idea, but 
his opponent is too tough.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:50.870
When Jack's Red Dragon 
Archfiend attacks, its effect

00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:54.120
destroys all his opponent's 
monsters in defense position.

00:15:57.400 --> 00:15:58.910
My turn!

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:02.360
I summon Battle Fader!

00:16:05.410 --> 00:16:11.990
Level 3 Sword Master tunes Level 1 Battle 
Fader and Level 4 Twin-Sword Marauder!

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:15.590
The pulse of the King now forms a line here!

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:18.270
Witness the power of the rumbling heavens!

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.450
Synchro Summon!

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:24.490
My soul!  Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:26.260
There it is!

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:31.440
It's Jack Atlas's ace monster 
Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:36.080
3000 attack points!

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:40.020
A rare card!

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:44.710
Red Dragon Archfiend attacks 
Hand-Holding Genie!

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:45.950
Yoshi!

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:48.180
Absolute Powerforce!

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:51.020
I activate the trap Castle Walls!

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:58.520
A monster in defense position gains 500 
defense points until the End Phase!

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:04.290
What?

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:11.440
No way!

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:15.750
He repelled Red Dragon Archfiend's attack!

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:18.880
His strategy focuses on 
gaining defense points.

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:22.750
All right, Yoshi!  Don't 
lose against a rare card!

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:26.890
How dare you!

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:31.190
But when Red Dragon Archfiend attacks 
a monster in defense position...

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:35.330
...all monsters on the field in 
defense position are destroyed!

00:17:35.980 --> 00:17:37.640
Demon Meteor!

00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:41.640
I activate the Continuous Trap Scrum Force!

00:17:42.130 --> 00:17:45.910
When there are two or more monsters 
in defense position on my field...

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:50.350
...my monsters in defense position can't be 
destroyed by spells, traps or monster effects!

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:55.560
He stopped him again!

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:59.240
I'm impressed that he's surviving 
using those monsters.

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:03.010
I end my turn!

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:09.380
Now it's my turn!

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:12.960
I activate Speed World 2's effect!

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:14.160
What?

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:16.550
I remove 4 Speed Counters.

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:20.900
For every Speed Spell in my hand, 
you take 800 points of damage!

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:29.950
Then I summon Kurama in defense position!

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:40.290
Due to Hand-Holding Genie's effect, it gains 
defense points equal to Kurama's defense points!

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:42.940
I end my turn!

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:45.540
I see what he's doing.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.770
He uses Hand-Holding 
Genie to protect himself.

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:51.470
Then he uses Speed World 
2 to deal effect damage.

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:54.430
That's Team Taiyo's basic strategy.

00:18:54.890 --> 00:19:00.480
According to the tournament rules, the Field 
Spell Speed World 2 can't be destroyed.

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:04.410
Therefore, he can comfortably 
activate its effect.

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:11.150
And with the Continuous Trap Scrum Force, he's 
preventing Red Dragon Archfiend's destruction effect.

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:13.620
My turn!

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:18.590
Since I can't destroy your monsters, 
I'll attack you directly!

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:22.140
I'll show you how to use 
Speed Spells correctly!

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:25.100
I activate Speed Spell - Sonic Buster!

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:29.950
When I have 4 or more Speed 
Counters, you take damage

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:33.360
equal to half the attack points 
of one monster on my field!

00:19:37.120 --> 00:19:38.220
Yoshi!

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:39.320
He did it!

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:42.630
Now it's 2600 life points versus 2500.

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:44.200
Jack caught up!

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:49.570
I set one card and end my turn!

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:53.150
Solely focusing on defense only goes so far.

00:19:53.150 --> 00:19:55.630
They'll change their strategy soon.

00:19:56.180 --> 00:19:57.430
My turn!

00:19:57.430 --> 00:19:58.620
I draw!

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:01.940
I summon Eyearmor in defense position!

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:11.550
He raised his defense points again.

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:13.680
I end my turn!

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:15.960
You're still using the same strategy?

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:17.670
Can't you do anything else?

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:20.540
Ignore them, Jin.

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:25.340
No matter what anyone says, this 
is our only battle strategy.

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:31.140
You'll only survive until 
I destroy your defense!

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:32.590
My turn!

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:36.310
I activate the trap Fiendish Chain!

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:40.960
The effect of one of your 
monsters is negated!

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:42.770
